From 7cc360a0a3deae1301366acb250e6bb1914895a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:14:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_tasks_panel: list the rows in pages, 10 by default,
 size changeable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.20 (ask 40). The panel's list is virtualized, so a
long history never cost render time, but the operator asked for visible
pages: 10 rows a page, with the size changeable.

A footer under the list: ‹ and › with "11–20 of 134" between them, and a
"10 per page" menu offering 10, 25, 50 and 100. A page counts task rows,
not thread headers; a thread whose rows cross a page break shows its
header on both pages, so no row is drawn without its thread. Pages slice
what the filters chose, in the panel's newest-first order, so a task that
starts lands on page 1. A filter change, typed or toggled, returns to page
1; a page past the end (rows deleted under it) clamps to the last; a turn
scrolls the list to its top. The size is saved with the panel's state
under its own key, beside the dock position, and a saved size the menu no
longer offers falls back to 10.

groups() stays the whole filtered list: bulk actions and the selection
read it, so a selection can span pages. shown_groups() is the page.

Two existing tests read a list longer than the dock and now ask for a
100-row page, which still holds all their rows (rename_vanish: 120 rows,
the assertion now ">= 100 lines"; scrollbar: 60 rows). Without that, the
scrollbar tests still passed, but no longer for the reason they state.

Tests: panel::pagination::tests (a split thread's header repeats and a
page counts rows; past the end is the last page; an empty list; a saved
size the menu does not offer) and panel::pagination_tests (10, 10 and 3
of 23; a filter change returns to page 1; the footer's › turns the page;
a new size returns to page 1). The three that depend on slicing were seen
failing with paginate made to return every row.
---

